Subject: [PATCH 41/90] Compile the shpool fixture prelude only in unit tests

Production expands the probe prelude directly through the macro. The old private constant is referenced only by the cfg(test) regression module, so exclude that fixture constant from normal library builds while retaining every script/kill regression. This fixes the upstream CI -D warnings failure without changing compiler flags, suppressing lints, or altering runtime scripts.

diff --git a/crates/project/src/terminals.rs b/crates/project/src/terminals.rs
index cd9b352032..c48fc1ac35 100644
--- a/crates/project/src/terminals.rs
+++ b/crates/project/src/terminals.rs
@@ -155,7 +155,8 @@ fi
     };
 }
 
-/// Prelude searching for shpool binary and socket path.
+/// Prelude searching for shpool binary and socket path in script regressions.
+#[cfg(test)]
 const SHPOOL_SCRIPT_PRELUDE: &str = shpool_script_prelude!("0");
 
 /// Prelude used for destructive operations, which must fail when shpool is unavailable.
